<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19930" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">grăvēdo</span></b> ,
			ĭnis, f.
		gravis. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Heaviness</i> of the limbs, <i>cold</i> in the head, <i>catarrh</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quasi gravedo profluat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. As. 4, 1, 51</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Cels. 4, 2, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Att.
				10, 16, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">16, 14, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cat. 44,
			13</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 23, 1, 6, § 10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">25, 13, 94, §
			150</span></i>; <i><span class="en">30, 4, 11,
				§ 31</span></i>.—In plur., <i><span class="en">Cels. 1,
			2</span></i>; of <i>heaviness in the head produced by
				intoxication</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ad crapulae gravedines,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					20, 13, 51, § 136</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Pregnancy</i>, <i><span class="en">Nemes. Cyneg.
				132</span></i>.</div>
